{"id":"000W4Y","title":"Parquet Flooring [Chaos Sudoku, Voxas, Ambiguous JSS & Kropki with SennyK]","author":"Malrog","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-20T13:03:50+00:00","posted":"Heute, 13:35 Uhr","rules":"SennyK and I set this puzzle together as part of a setting competition organised by mnasti2, where collaborators didn't know who they were setting with!\n\nThe theme was (appropriately) Ambiguity/Duality and after spending some time evolving this ruleset, we are very happy with the final result. We hope you enjoy uncovering what it has to offer, and look forward to reading your comments. Thank you for your time.\n\nRules\n\nNormal Chaos Construction rules apply: Place the digits from 1 to 9 in every row, column and edge-connected 9-cell region. Regions must be determined by the solver.\n\n(Ambiguous) Kropki Dots: Digits in cells separated by a white dot must be consecutive. Digits in cells separated by a black dot must be in a 1:2 ratio. Digits in cells separated by a grey dot are either consecutive, or in a 1:2 ratio, or both.\n\nNormal Voxas rules apply: Divide the grid into two types of rectangle, 1x2 and 1x3. White dots separate rectangles with the same size and orientation. Black dots separate rectangles with neither the same size nor the same orientation. Grey dots separate rectangles with either the same size or the same orientation, but not both.\n\nInteraction: Each rectangle must be entirely contained within a single region.\n\nAmbiguous Japanese Sums: Clues outside the grid give the sums of digits in the contiguous sequences of cells belonging to one rectangle type in the respective row or column in the correct order. Digits in the other rectangle type serve as delimeters between the groups. It is up to the solver to determine which rectangle type is summed in each clued row and column. An asterisk (∗) clue shows an arbitrary number of clues, which can be zero. A question mark may represent any digit from 0 to 9, but for double digit numbers, the first digit may not be 0.\n\nSolve on Penpa\n\nSolve on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Column 8, top to bottom, with a - separator for each region border.","tags":["Sudoku","Japanische Summen","Kropki Pairs (Variante)","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/ye69ttaz","kind":"short"},{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/e1m41rdevx","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/e1m41rdevx","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":12,"cols":12,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-20T13:03:50+00:00"}